From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 19 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: losses, win and draw for n > 2, team LP,
 Debug.EliminateDuelist

Losses, win and draw for duels with more than 2 duelists (phase 2, T5A).

LP sites: 10 reads and writes of player[p].lp now go through lp_ref(p)
(RELOAD_FIELD, Duel.GetLP, Duel.SetLP, QueryField, Damage x4 with the
match kill test, Recover, PayLPCost check). lp_ref(p) is
player[team_of(p)].lp, and team == seat with 1, 2, 3 or 4 duelists that
are not Tag, so the value is the same as before for every p. Left as
they are because the Domain patch anchors their text: check_lp_cost
(field.cpp) and PayLPCost step 1 `lp -= cost` (operations.cpp). Setup
writes and the relay reset are not changed either.

New field::check_losses_n(), called from Adjust step 1 only when
n_duelists > 2. It waits while a chain resolves or a script runs. A team
loses by LP (no living member has CANNOT_LOSE_LP), by deck (per member),
by pending_loss or by Duel.Win of another team. No team left = MSG_WIN
(DUELIST_NONE = 0xFF, reason). One team left = MSG_WIN(team, reason), and free for all
sends MSG_DUELIST_ELIMINATED (200) for each loser first. More teams left
= eliminate(p, reason) per loser in turn order from the turn player.
Every duelist is marked eliminated at the end of a duel, so MSG_WIN is
sent once.

Stock blocks: break_effect win block gets n_duelists == 2 &&, Adjust
step 1 is if(n_duelists > 2) check_losses_n(); else stock. The match
kill message is only for n_duelists == 2.

Duel.Win for n > 2: accepts a living seat, needs a living opponent
without CANNOT_LOSE_EFFECT, the first call wins. The stock text is not
changed for 2 duelists. Debug.EliminateDuelist(p, reason) sets
player_info::pending_loss (new, 0x100 | reason), Lua error unless
n > 2 and p is alive. Debug.SetupDuelists rejects DUEL_RELAY and
DUEL_INVERTED_QUICK_PRIORITY when n > 2.

before_first_attack_turn: 2 duelists and Tag keep the stock test. Free
for all is true while a living duelist has had no turn and during the
first turn of the turn player.

field::eliminate(p, reason) is declared as T5B needs it. Here it is a
stub that only sets eliminated. common.h gets the ids 200, 201, 202.

Every duelist value that reaches lp_ref comes from a check with
is_duelist (GetLP, SetLP, Damage, Recover, CheckLPCost, PayLPCost) or from
a loop. Two duelists are unchanged: every changed stock statement is guarded by
n_duelists == 2 or is the same value as before. Left for T5B: the body of
eliminate. The wrapper and the TS side read message 200.

